                            <comment id="476645" author="paf0186" created="Wed, 29 Oct 2025 22:53:56 +0000">&lt;p&gt;With the shift to ec-as-mirror, we get most of this for free.  We should still do some testing probably, but there's one thing remaining.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19527" title="FLR-EC: Never select EC mirror as primary for write or allow setting PREFER flags" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19527"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19527&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; will prevent selecting a parity/EC mirror as write destination, but it could still be selected for read.  In that case, we can't read from the parity components and must switch to another mirror.  This is probably almost the same code as the patch which makes old clients avoid components with unknown patterns (The one referenced in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19520" title="FLR-EC: Don't read parity components on old clients" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19520"&gt;LU-19520&lt;/a&gt; ), just here it would avoid components with PARITY set.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="478410" author="gerrit" created="Fri, 14 Nov 2025 23:37:15 +0000">&lt;p&gt;"Patrick Farrell &amp;lt;pfarrell@whamcloud.com&amp;gt;" uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/62539" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/62539&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Subject: &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19481" title="FLR-EC: Basic do-no-harm lov IO support" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19481"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19481&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; lov: skip parity mirrors for normal read/write IOs&lt;br/&gt;
